  "_comment": "Real-catalog config. Originally 12 oc-go + 4 kimi models verified 2026-05-25. POLICY 2026-05-28 (kit-owner whitelist): only the newest model per family is shipped enabled — glm-5.1 (premium quality), kimi-k2.6 (premium quality, kimi-direct only — opencode-go duplicate disabled to avoid path drift), qwen3.7-max (standard tier, fast+cheap). Everything else is disabled by default. Server has respect_requested_model: true; the .model field in responses is unreliable (upstream-naming quirks: minimax echoes as \"MiniMax-M2.7\"; deepseek may echo as another name) — the router log is the source of truth, NOT the response.model. Consumers can re-enable any disabled model locally but the shipped default is the whitelist.",
